At 12:24 AM 07/11/2001 -0400, Pierre Abbat wrote:
>I'm going to add a page about money and banks to the phrasebook. Which is the
>better word for changing money, basygau or galfi?

Huh?  Assuming that I know what you mean by the phrase, it is 
neither.  galfi lo jdini would be more like debasing currency by adding 
cheap metals to the coinage.

canja is the correct root, and changing money is something like seldi'i canja.

